+{"q": 118, "question": "Who is the most likely murderer?", "narrative": "When the grisly sight of Hugo's lifeless body, axed to death at a campground, meets Detective Winston's eyes, he finds himself entangled in an unnerving hunt for the truth between two suspects - Salvador and Wade.\n\nDetective Winston sat busily in his office, perusing online photos of mountain climbing adventures typical of suspect Wade. Eyeing the images, it became immediately apparent among the ropes, carabiners, and pitons that Wade always had one particular piece of gear with him - an axe. Along with the axe, a curious detail drew his attention - a blue bead bracelet that Wade wore on every climb.\n\nAs Winston was engrossed in his photographic search, his assistant entered the room, her eyes teary. \"Detective, I confronted Wade about my bracelet, the one he keeps wearing,\" she said, noticeably upset. \"He brushed me off, claiming that it became a necessary memento from an infamous climbing adventure with him.\" \n\nScratchy phone recorded deductions hung in the air as a woman's voice filled the room, \"Hugo was said to have checked into the campground... the same day as Wade.\"\n\nWinston tapped the ash from his cigarette into an old coffee mug and decided it was time to have a little chat with Mr. Wade. \n\nPulling up to the nearby climbing spot, which was also a well-known campground, he found Wade wiping the sweat off his brow as he examined a climbing route, axe handle sticking out from his backpack. The seasoned detective noted that they were at the plot adjacent to where Hugo had camped.\n\nWade looked up, seeing Winston step out of his car. \"Hey, detective... what brings you out here?\"\n\nWinston crossed his arms, gaze lingering on the axe handle. \"Thought it was time we had a chat.\"\n\nWade chuckled, adjusting the strap of the blue bead bracelet that was hanging loosely on his wrist, \"Alright then, shoot.\"\n\nWinston observed the bracelet, recognizing it from the pictures